title The widening answered from underneath, and a family that split in two
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, deep-read one council-rota row, send the finished increment
think Council rota row 4 (Earth - Mercury) read: the one-clock naming law, Two Rooms, the marked value. Two Rooms governed the whole lap -- the predicted fall was a claim until the scan measured it, so the prediction was written down first and the meter was the only thing allowed to close it.
think sibling_waits led the queue at 420 with a price of eighty-six, and reading the price by kind showed it was forty-three import bindings of mask.rye plus forty-three openings of a private waits.
think mask.rye is imported by the harness at its own head, so those forty-three cost nothing, exactly as carry.rye did last lap.
think The forty-three function openings were the real question. Publishing a helper each rung deliberately kept private widens an API in a way the Finished opening did not, since Finished already stood in a published signature and waits stands in none.
think So the move was to lift waits too. The rung stub for waits stays PRIVATE -- it answers its own module's callers exactly as the body did -- and the harness body serves the lifted sibling_waits. Nothing is published anywhere.
think Measured the waits family before touching anything: forty-six rungs hold one identical body, three more than the caller family. Those three turned out to be exactly the three that cannot or should not fold -- confer.rye and entrust.rye stand below the fold line, and revoke.rye keeps its Table private.
think Predicted the fall in two parts before the lift: 420 for the caller by the arc's formula, and 89 for the helper, being 225 carried before less 126 in stubs and 10 left standing among the three home rungs. Measured 509 exactly.
obs A caller reaching a private helper prices as a widening only while the helper stays in the rung. The meter is honest and the price is real, yet it is a price on one particular ordering of the work. Lift the helper first and it vanishes. Gall's Law, read this lap, says the same thing in its own words -- grow the thing from underneath rather than designing the door.
obs The fold line and the private-Table rung name exactly the same three rungs. That coincidence is what made the lap free, and it is a coincidence rather than a rule, so the next family of this shape must be measured the same way rather than assumed.
obs One number rose. Carrying families 703 to 704, because the helper family split into the forty-three stubs and the three rungs still writing the body between themselves. A number climbing in a fold arc reads as alarm until it is read, and this one says a family divided rather than that carry came back.
obs The spelled-number loom caught its own author again: a sentence reading "forty-three rungs ... and the three that stayed home" was read as forty-five, since the reader joins spelled numbers across "and". Correct behavior on an honest sentence, and the sentence was rewritten rather than the guard loosened.
